      "side": 1,
      "message": "After a successful `aom_codec_decode()` call, we usually call `aom_codec_get_frame()` as follows only once:\n\n```\n    aom_codec_iter_t iter \u003d nullptr;\n    aom_image_t *img \u003d nullptr;\n    while ((img \u003d aom_codec_get_frame(\u0026dec, \u0026iter)) !\u003d nullptr) {\n      // Use img.\n    }\n```\n\nSo this test calls `aom_codec_get_frame()` in an unusual (but legal) way. Still, I am surprised that the fix is that large.\n\nThe commit message says:\n\n```\nadd_grain_if_needed() took the next slot of\ngrain_image_frame_buffers[MAX_NUM_SPATIAL_LAYERS] from a counter that\ngrew on every aom_codec_get_frame() call and was reset only by the next\ndecode call.\n```\n\nIt seems that we can make the bug fix smaller if we can reset this counter whenever `aom_codec_get_frame()` is called with `iter \u003d nullptr`. I took a quick look. Something like the following seems to work:\n\n```\ndiff --git a/av1/av1_dx_iface.c b/av1/av1_dx_iface.c\nindex 3fbe5e53f2..f57b48d59e 100644\n--- a/av1/av1_dx_iface.c\n+++ b/av1/av1_dx_iface.c\n@@ -577,13 +577,6 @@ static void release_pending_output_frames(aom_codec_alg_priv_t *ctx) {\n     }\n     pbi-\u003enum_output_frames \u003d 0;\n     unlock_buffer_pool(pool);\n-    for (size_t j \u003d 0; j \u003c ctx-\u003enum_grain_image_frame_buffers; j++) {\n-      pool-\u003erelease_fb_cb(pool-\u003ecb_priv, \u0026ctx-\u003egrain_image_frame_buffers[j]);\n-      ctx-\u003egrain_image_frame_buffers[j].data \u003d NULL;\n-      ctx-\u003egrain_image_frame_buffers[j].size \u003d 0;\n-      ctx-\u003egrain_image_frame_buffers[j].priv \u003d NULL;\n-    }\n-    ctx-\u003enum_grain_image_frame_buffers \u003d 0;\n   }\n }\n \n@@ -842,6 +835,16 @@ static aom_image_t *decoder_get_frame(aom_codec_alg_priv_t *ctx,\n     frame_worker_data-\u003ereceived_frame \u003d 0;\n     check_resync(ctx, frame_worker_data-\u003epbi);\n   }\n+  if (*index \u003d\u003d 0) {\n+    BufferPool *const pool \u003d ctx-\u003ebuffer_pool;\n+    for (size_t j \u003d 0; j \u003c ctx-\u003enum_grain_image_frame_buffers; j++) {\n+      pool-\u003erelease_fb_cb(pool-\u003ecb_priv, \u0026ctx-\u003egrain_image_frame_buffers[j]);\n+      ctx-\u003egrain_image_frame_buffers[j].data \u003d NULL;\n+      ctx-\u003egrain_image_frame_buffers[j].size \u003d 0;\n+      ctx-\u003egrain_image_frame_buffers[j].priv \u003d NULL;\n+    }\n+    ctx-\u003enum_grain_image_frame_buffers \u003d 0;\n+  }\n   YV12_BUFFER_CONFIG *sd;\n   aom_film_grain_t *grain_params;\n   if (av1_get_raw_frame(frame_worker_data-\u003epbi, *index, \u0026sd, \u0026grain_params) !\u003d\n```",
      "revId": "fb8a3422af1913d4ed55807ad299005d629337bb",
